    {
      "id": "fb-002",
      "question": "How are SIM bundles managed?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 20.22,
      "answer": "SIM bundles are managed through various strategies to ensure consistent service quality and efficient billing. The management includes:\n\n1. **Regional Billing Plan**: This plan involves different pricing strategies for local movement, cross-border activities, and high-roaming fleets. It uses local SIM billing policies, roaming policies, IoT SIM bundles, and integration with satellite services like Iridium.\n\n2. **SIM & Connectivity Infrastructure**: This supports local SIMs, multi-SIM configurations, roaming detection, automated usage alerts, and AI-based billing risk detection.\n\n3. **Multi-SIM Bundle Rules**: These rules help manage unmonitored SIM usage and roaming by enforcing SIM policies and sending automated usage alerts.\n\nThese procedures are part of the approved company procedures for sales in Uganda and Kenya.\n\nSource: Sales Procedures 3DS-QMS-PR-09 ver26 (Uganda & Kenya) — this is the documented procedure.",
