    {
      "id": "fb-005",
      "question": "How do tracking tokens work?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 22.06,
      "answer": "Tracking tokens in the NAVAS ecosystem are used to pay for GPS tracking based on time. They are billed per hour, day, or month, allowing you to pay only when your assets are active. The system supports pausing and resuming, so you can manage token usage efficiently. Tokens are consumed on a first-in, first-out basis, meaning your oldest tokens are used first. You can check your token balance and manage your token queue through the OLIWA mobile app.\n\nSource: NAVAS Token Billing Strategy and OLIWA Mobile App Guide — these are the documented designs; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
