      "answer": "To create a new geofence in the OLIWA mobile app, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Open Geofences**: Tap the menu icon (☰) at the top left and choose \"Geofences,\" or tap \"Geofences\" under Quick actions on the dashboard.\n2. **Stay on the Zones tab** and tap \"New\" at the bottom right.\n3. **Choose the shape**:\n   - **Polygon**: An area with corners. You need at least 4 points.\n   - **Line**: A route or road. You need at least 2 points.\n   - **Circle**: A center and a radius.\n   - Note: Switching shape clears the points you have placed.\n4. **Tap the map to place the shape**:\n   - For a **Polygon** or **Line**: Tap each corner or point in turn. The hint at the top counts them, e.g., \"3 points — tap Save when done.\" Tap \"Undo\" to remove the last point.\n   - For a **Circle**: Tap once to place the center, then set the size with the Radius slider, one of the presets (100 m, 500 m, 1 km, 5 km, 10 km, 50 km, 100 km), or tap the radius value and type it in meters (between 50 m and 100,000 m).\n5. **Tap Save & attach**: It stays greyed out until the shape has enough points.\n6. In **New Geofence**, enter:\n   - **Name**: At least 5 characters, e.g., \"Head Office.\"\n   - **Description**: At least 6 characters: what the zone is for.\n7. **Tap Create**.\n\nOnce created, you'll see \"Geofence created,\" and the zone will appear on the map and in the list. The app will then open \"Attach devices to your zone\" so you can choose which vehicles it watches. You can skip this step and attach them later if you prefer.",
